I tested the agent in five chat conversations. Every call took the expected path and reached the right end, but the closing sentences could not be seen in chat: a turn that ends the call returns a 502 error. I made one fix and re-saved under the slot `final` (version 2).

**The fix:** in the first chat check, the caller's card choice made the call reload the card list and ask again which card. The silent loading step at the start was saying "Bilgilerinizi kontrol ediyorum."; I removed that line and the call now continues normally. The trade-off is that the agent no longer says that sentence while it waits, including during the 12-second balance answer for customer 94907600.

**Chat tests (call date 12 October 2026):**

| Customer | Scenario | Result |
|---|---|---|
| 97526380 | Three cards (like Example 3) | Asked which card with two of the caller's own card names, read only Yıldız Premium (22.500 TL, minimum 9.000 TL, due 15 Ekim 2026), asked about another card, then made the offer |
| 96158684 | Statement week change (Examples 2 and 5) | Read the debt, current week and next dates; asked again after "Olur herhalde"; changed to week 3 once after "Evet" with dates 16 Kasım 2026 / 26 Kasım 2026; ended to the main menu |
| 96125950 | Asks for card digits, no e-mail on file (Example 6) | Refused the first twelve and first six digits; offered only the statement date change |
| 95004361 | Debt reading, then "teşekkürler" (Example 1) | Reading matched the worked example word for word; ended to the main menu |
| 94835408 | Statement week service fails | Went to the end node that says "Şu anda hesap kesim tarihinizi değiştiremiyorum, sizi müşteri temsilcimize aktarıyorum." |

**Still to know:**
- **Closing sentences:** because of the 502, I could not see a closing sentence being spoken. I confirmed from the call events that each call reached the right end node, and the sentences are fixed text in those nodes. A simulation would confirm they are spoken.
- **Untested paths:** I did not test in chat the e-mail send, two cards with the same name and last four digits, joint statements, third-party callers, silence, or anger.
- **Small wording drift:** once the model paraphrased the week options sentence ("veya" instead of "ya da").

